2026-09-12 adaptive allocation: no filler clips just to hit a number; editorial safety ceiling is 8/source and 20 total
2026-09-12 memory architecture fix: full 256x144/6fps semantic analysis runs only in analysis stage; render consumes approved allocation directly
2026-09-12 storage architecture fix: each allocated clip gets an isolated GitHub workspace, renders one MP4, uploads that video immediately as its own artifact, uploads QA metadata separately, deletes source/output locally, then the next clip starts; max-parallel=1
2026-09-12 MediaSilo fix: each official reel is resolved/downloaded/verified once in analysis, staged as a 1-day source artifact, and reused by isolated render workspaces; render jobs never resolve MediaSilo or install Chromium
2026-09-12 quality fix: isolated one-clip workspaces are retained for stability, but low-bitrate shadow encoding is no longer used for qualification artifacts
2026-09-12 OOM root-cause fix: far-apart montage segments are extracted independently with bounded decoding, staged losslessly as FFV1/PCM, stitched into a short local source, then passed to the canonical final-quality renderer; no full-reel multi-trim buffering or render-time source-structure rescan
2026-09-12 CFR fix: final canonical renderer explicitly normalizes output to 60000/1001 CFR after lossless staging and bounds filter/x264 threading; QA reports actual frame rates on failure
2026-09-12 FFmpeg compatibility fix: CFR uses -r 60000/1001 plus -vsync cfr so Ubuntu22 FFmpeg 4.4 and Ubuntu24 FFmpeg 6 share the same final encoder path; exact frame-rate QA remains fail-closed
2026-09-12 source-master fix: MediaSilo fileSize is validated as integer KiB metadata with a strict [KiB*1024, KiB*1024+1024) byte range; type=source, SHA256, geometry and 60000/1001 checks remain fail-closed
2026-09-12 source-fidelity fix: destructive digital zoom/crop-upscale effect paths are disabled in isolated final renders; approved semantic timing/story is rendered source-native full-frame
2026-09-12 fidelity-QA root-cause correction: previous SSIM/PSNR compared two separately rendered CFR timelines, so one-frame timing differences in fast gameplay produced false ~0.90 SSIM/~22 dB results. The pipeline now renders the approved source-native edit exactly once to a canonical lossless FFV1 60000/1001 master, encodes the 250 Mbps H.264 directly from that master without rebuilding cuts/timing, requires exact decoded frame-count/geometry/fps equality, resets PTS on both inputs, then enforces SSIM >= 0.99 and PSNR >= 40 dB. No threshold reduction.
2026-09-13 exact-fps container fix: Matroska's 1 ms time base rationalized 60000/1001 to 19001/317 even though reference/output frame counts matched. The canonical FFV1/PCM master now uses NUT, which preserves the exact 60000/1001 rational time base; final H.264 encodes directly from that same master. Fidelity thresholds remain unchanged.
2026-09-13 end-to-end fidelity hardening: every original MediaSilo source interval is now decoded and frame-hashed against its FFV1/NUT staged segment; hashes and frame counts must match exactly before editing. Source pixel format, SAR, color range/space/transfer/primaries and chroma location are carried through staging, canonical master and final H.264 and must match at QA. No crop/scale/zoom, no silent chroma conversion, SSIM >= 0.99 and PSNR >= 40 dB remain mandatory.
2026-09-13 lossless transport correction: FFmpeg NUT cannot serialize the required BT.709 range/space/transfer/primaries/chroma metadata. Staging and canonical masters now use libx264 -qp 0 in MOV with explicit H.264 VUI plus video_track_timescale=60000. CI preflights exact decoded hashes, 60000/1001 fps, 1/60000 time base, unspecified SAR, yuv420p, tv range, BT.709 signaling and left chroma siting before any MediaSilo download; all existing strict fidelity gates remain enabled.
2026-09-13 run37 correction: adaptive allocation self-test is FFmpeg-free again; render workers retain the lossless transport preflight. Canonical pixel hashes are now generated after the same 60000/1001 CFR scheduling and duration bound used by the lossless master, preventing speed-edited segments from comparing a pre-CFR frame sequence against a post-CFR encode. Fidelity thresholds and exact decoded-pixel checks remain unchanged.
2026-09-13 semantic hardening: source segments must be monotonic and non-overlapping; verified Finishing Moves may continue only into strictly later gameplay inside the configured gap and may not fall back to earlier footage. Duplicate detection unions every explicit payoff anchor and rejects reused semantic-montage moments. Allocation is quality-first rather than cardinality-first. Pure-Python self-tests lock these regressions before source download.
